  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Frequency",
   "texto": [
    "In a simple phrase in present, **toujours** (always), **souvent** (often) and **parfois** (sometimes) usually go **después del verbo conjugado**: **Je vais souvent au cinéma**.",
    "«Never.» is **ne … jamais**, which replaces «ne … pas»: **Je ne travaille jamais le dimanche**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Two irregular verbs",
   "texto": [
    "**Aller** (go) and **faire** (do) are irregular and very used.",
    "In **Je vais au cinéma**, **à + le** (le cinéma) is contracted in **au**. In **à la piscine**, the preposition and feminine are kept separate.",
    "**Faire du sport** = doing sport."
   ]
  },
